{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Cite and design refresh against origin/main 2e28d817a7e (the first comment's audit basis 083620b0 predates 9510ecf2629 \"Narrow ready ticket discovery\", d91def6dfa0 \"Settle stale gate handles\", and 4f12815e9a0 \"Condense core library and MCP comments\"). The description is rewritten on this tip; corrections to the first two comments:\n\n1. ready_tickets: 9510ecf added `ready_ticket_summary.schema.json` (`additionalProperties: false`) and `ReadyTicketSummaryOut`; the tool returns lean summary rows by default and `ticket_state` rows with `full=true`. Its advertised schema is therefore `{\"result\": {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\": {\"anyOf\": [ready_ticket_summary, ticket_state]}}}`, not `list_of ticket_state`; a single schema would make the lowlevel validator reject one of the two modes. The coverage test already maps `ready_tickets -> READY_TICKET_SUMMARY`; the canonical diff test compares against the two-schema `anyOf`.\n2. Model inventory is now 33 public models in 558 LOC (was 32 / 619). The mapped/unmapped audit adds `ReadyTicketSummaryOut` (mapped to `ready_ticket_summary`); every other row of the first comment's audit stands.\n3. Release note (second comment): lean `ready_tickets` rows no longer carry mirror-restored keys today (9510ecf already narrowed them), so the \"on lean list rows the mirror-restored description, comments, deps, ...\" sentence applies to `list_tickets` rows only.\n4. Moved cites: `install_error_guard` `_mcp_errors.py:77-133` (was 88-138); `tool_annotation_presets` `_mcp_models.py:524-558` (was 585-619); `_OmitUnsetOut` `_mcp_models.py:35-50` (was 49-69); `_ack`/`_with_push` `_mcp_writes.py:85-110`; `_structured_llm_failure` `_mcp_llm.py:20-37` (was 28-50); `_mcp_llm.py` import of `tool_annotation_presets` `:16` (was 24); `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` `_mcp_health.py:51-52` (was 72-73); `test_mcp_http_transport.py:536,834-839`; `_wire_bytes` docstring `_mcp_budget.py:96-101`; `gen_mcp_reference.py` `dump=` at `:96` (was 69) and model-field wording `:205-212`; CI step `MCP model schema drift gate` at `_build-and-test.yml:845-850` (was 765-773); `docs/output-schemas.md:232-234`; `check_mcp_models.MODEL_SCHEMAS` at `:25`. Unchanged: `mcp_server.py:413-419,598,608-609,684`, `_mcp_serving.py:103,121,137-138`, `pyproject.toml:583`.\n5. Precedent for the four new `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS` keys: `review_code_gate` (`schemas/__init__.py:171`); `enrich`/`overlap_judge` are still present but slated for deletion by another epic.\n6. AC 1's grep also matches the frozen plan-review eval fixture `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/eval_specs/plan-review-E6.eval.yaml` (recorded ticket text, not code); it stays unedited and the AC now excludes `docs/experiments/` alongside `tests/fixtures/`."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792380171294019001,"uuid":"dd231c11-1f96-4f00-9a97-bbfaff532bbe"}